  "output": "Based on the provided files (and consistent with prior audits already in memory), here's a focused analysis with concrete fixes.\n\n## 1. Caching opportunities\n\n**`src/utils/cache.ts`** — the cache helpers exist but aren't used to their potential:\n- `pruneOldCache()` runs synchronously on module load (line 30, top-level call), iterating all of `localStorage` — fine at current scale, but it's a side effect on import, which makes this module untestable/impure and re-runs on every page load. Move it into an explicit `initCache()` called once from `main.tsx`.\n- No TTL/expiry on cached values — `cacheGet` returns stale data forever until overwritten. Add a timestamp wrapper:\n\n```ts\ntype Cached<T> = { value: T; savedAt: number };\n\nexport function cacheSet<T>(key: string, value: T) {\n  try {\n    window.localStorage.setItem(`${CACHE_PREFIX}${key}`, JSON.stringify({ value, savedAt: Date.now() } as Cached<T>));\n  } catch {}\n}\n\nexport function cacheGet<T>(key: string, fallback: T, maxAgeMs = Infinity): T {\n  try {\n    const raw = window.localStorage.getItem(`${CACHE_PREFIX}${key}`);\n    if (!raw) return fallback;\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw) as Cached<T>;\n    if (Date.now() - parsed.savedAt > maxAgeMs) return fallback;\n    return parsed.value;\n  } catch {\n    return fallback;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**`src/api.ts`** — every `request()` call hits the network with no dedup/memoization. Bots, campaigns, phrases, outcomes, language settings are all fairly static reference data fetched repeatedly across views. Add a short-lived in-memory cache keyed by path for GETs:\n\n```ts\nconst inflightGets = new Map<string, Promise<unknown>>();\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const isGet = !options.method || options.method === 'GET';\n  if (isGet && inflightGets.has(path)) return inflightGets.get(path) as Promise<T>;\n  const promise = doRequest<T>(path, options).finally(() => inflightGets.delete(path));\n  if (isGet) inflightGets.set(path, promise);\n  return promise;\n}\n```\nThis dedupes concurrent identical requests (common when multiple components mount and call `api.campaigns()` at once) without needing a full cache invalidation story.\n\n## 2. Redundant computations\n\n**`src/utils/transcript.ts`** `buildConversationItems` — recomputes `inlineEvents` filter + two sorts on every call. If this is called from a render path per transcript (likely in `TranscriptsView`, noted in memory obs 1389), wrap the call site in `useMemo(() => buildConversationItems(transcript, events), [transcript, events])` rather than fixing the function itself — the function is pure and cheap per-call, the win is avoiding recompute on unrelated re-renders.\n\n**`src/utils/formatting.ts`** `parseApiDate` — regex-tests then constructs a `Date` on every call; `formatDate`/`formatTime`/`timeAgo` each call it independently for the same value in places that display both date and time for a single record (e.g., a transcript row showing both `formatDate(created_at)` and `timeAgo(created_at)`). Minor, but if these are in a list of hundreds of rows, memoize per-row with `useMemo` keyed on the row's timestamp rather than recomputing per formatter call.\n\n## 3. Unnecessary React re-renders\n\n**`src/hooks/useToasts.ts`** — solid already (uses `useCallback`, functional state updates). No issue.\n\n**`src/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts`** — good pattern (refs to avoid re-subscribing). No issue.\n\nGiven the truncated file set, the concrete re-render risk flagged repeatedly in prior audits (obs 1395, 1612, 1614) is **inline object/array literals passed as props** in `App.tsx` and `CampaignsView` — e.g., a `dialing_strategy` or config object built fresh each render defeats `React.memo` on children. Since `App.tsx` wasn't included here, apply this pattern where it recurs:\n\n```tsx\n// Before: new object each render, breaks memo on <StrategyEditor strategy={...}/>\n<StrategyEditor strategy={{ ...campaign.dialing_strategy, outcome_rules: rules }} />\n\n// After\nconst strategy = useMemo(\n  () => ({ ...campaign.dialing_strategy, outcome_rules: rules }),\n  [campaign.dialing_strategy, rules]\n);\n<StrategyEditor strategy={strategy} />\n```\n\n## 4. Memory leaks\n\n**`src/hooks/useCountUp.ts`** — `requestAnimationFrame(tick)` loop has no cancellation on unmount. If `target` changes rapidly (e.g., a dashboard stat updating on poll) or the component unmounts mid-animation, the rAF callback still fires and calls `setState` on an unmounted component / stacks concurrent animations:\n\n```ts\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (target === 0) { setValue(0); return; }\n  let cancelled = false;\n  let rafId: number;\n  const start = performance.now();\n  ref.current?.classList.add('counting');\n  const tick = (now: number) => {\n    if (cancelled) return;\n    const progress = Math.min((now - start) / duration, 1);\n    const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - progress, 3);\n    setValue(Math.round(target * eased));\n    if (progress < 1) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    else ref.current?.classList.remove('counting');\n  };\n  rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n  return () => { cancelled = true; cancelAnimationFrame(rafId); };\n}, [target, duration]);\n```\n\n**`src/hooks/useToasts.ts`** — `setTimeout(() => dismissToast(id), durationMs)` (line 27) is never cleared. If the component unmounts before the timer fires, `dismissToast` calls `setState` on an unmounted host — React 18 tolerates this silently but it's still a dangling timer holding a closure. Track timeout ids and clear on unmount:\n\n```ts\nconst timeoutsRef = useRef<Set<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>>>(new Set());\nuseEffect(() => () => timeoutsRef.current.forEach(clearTimeout), []);\n// in showToast:\nif (durationMs > 0) {\n  const t = setTimeout(() => { dismissToast(id); timeoutsRef.current.delete(t); }, durationMs);\n  timeoutsRef.current.add(t);\n}\n```\n\n## 5. N+1 patterns\nNothing N+1-shaped is visible in this specific file set (no per-item fetch loops in `api.ts`'s excerpt). The N+1-relevant finding from prior audits — analytics endpoints doing in-memory aggregation instead of Mongo pipelines (obs 1609) — is backend, not in these frontend files; that stands as previously reported, not re-verified here.\n\n---\nNote: this substantially overlaps with prior audits already recorded (obs 1389–1396, 1611–1615) for this repo — the `useCountUp`/`useToasts` leak details and the `cache.ts` TTL gap are the new, file-specific items from this pass. Want me to implement any of these fixes directly?\n",
